A...","zh":"dk-breadcrumb-creator_SETUP_GUIDE - AIエージェント开发工具","ja":"dk-breadcrumb-creatorベストプラクティス - AIエージェントのワークフロー分析","ko":"dk-breadcrumb-creator_TROUBLESHOOTING - AI 에이전트 개발 키트","es":"Configuración de dk-breadcrumb-creator: Guía de Análisis ...","fr":"Mise en place de dk-breadcrumb-creator: Guide d''Analyse d...","de":"Einrichtung von dk-breadcrumb-creator: Workflow-Analyse-H...","pt":"dk-breadcrumb-creator: Guia de Configuração para Análise ...","ru":"dk-breadcrumb-creator: Руководство по настройке для анали...","ar":"dk-breadcrumb-creator: دليل الإعداد لتحليل تدفق العمل باس..."},"description":{"en":"Discover how dk-breadcrumb-creator simplifies debugging by tracing workflows through the harness-kit monorepo. Get started with setup and usage today!","zh":"了解dk-breadcrumb-creator的技术细节和应用场景，实现AIエージェント的高效开发和调试","ja":"dk-breadcrumb-creatorを使用してAIエージェントのワークフローを分析し、開発効率を向上させる","ko":"dk-breadcrumb-creator를 사용하여 AI 에이전트 개발의 어려움을 해결하고 효율성을 높여보세요","es":"Aprende a utilizar dk-breadcrumb-creator para analizar flujos de trabajo y depurar aplicaciones con tecnologías de agente de inteligencia artificial","fr":"Découvrez comment utiliser dk-breadcrumb-creator pour analyser les flux de travail et déboguer des applications avec des outils d''agent d''intelligence artifi...","de":"Erfahren Sie, wie Sie dk-breadcrumb-creator verwenden, um Workflows zu analysieren und Anwendungen mit KI-Agent-Technologien zu debuggen","pt":"Aprenda a configurar o dk-breadcrumb-creator para analisar fluxos de trabalho e identificar problemas com Ferramentas de Inteligência Artificial","ru":"Узнайте, как настроить dk-breadcrumb-creator для анализа рабочих процессов и выявления проблем с помощью ИИ Агентов","ar":"تعرف على كيفية تعيين dk-breadcrumb-creator لتحليل تدفقات العمل وتحديد المشكلات باستخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"},"definition":{"en":"dk-breadcrumb-creator is a workflow analysis tool that traces workflows through the harness-kit monorepo, producing a compact debugging reference.","zh":"dk-breadcrumb-creator是一种用于AIエージェント开发的工具，提供工作流程分析和调试功能","ja":"dk-breadcrumb-creatorはAIエージェントのワークフロー分析と開発を支援するツールです","ko":"dk-breadcrumb-creator는 AI 에이전트 개발을 위한 도구로 작업 흐름 분석과 디버깅 기능을 제공합니다","es":"dk-breadcrumb-creator es una herramienta de análisis de flujos de trabajo que utiliza inteligencia artificial para depurar aplicaciones","fr":"dk-breadcrumb-creator est un outil d''analyse de flux de travail qui utilise l''intelligence artificielle pour déboguer des applications","de":"dk-breadcrumb-creator ist ein Werkzeug zur Analyse von Workflows, das KI zur Fehlerbehebung von Anwendungen verwendet","pt":"O dk-breadcrumb-creator é uma ferramenta de análise de fluxo de trabalho que produz uma referência de depuração compacta","ru":"dk-breadcrumb-creator - это инструмент для анализа рабочих процессов, который производит компактную справку для отладки","ar":"dk-breadcrumb-creator هو أداة لتحليل تدفق العمل التي تنتج مرجعًا مدمجًا للتصحيح"},"features":{"en":["Traces workflows through the harness-kit monorepo","Produces a compact debugging reference for devs and agents","Supports workflow analysis via <flow_context> and $ARGUMENTS","Generates output for debugging purposes, not onboarding or architecture overviews"],"zh":["支持工作流程分析和调试","集成harness-kit monorepo","提供紧凑的调试参考输出","适用于开发人员和AIエージェント","支持多种工作流程跟踪"],"ja":["ワークフロー分析とデバッグをサポート","harness-kit monorepoと統合","コンパクトなデバッグリファレンス出力を提供","開発者とAIエージェント向け","複数のワークフロー追跡をサポート"],"ko":["작업 흐름 분석 및 디버깅 지원","harness-kit monorepo 통합","コンパクト한 디버깅 참조 출력 제공","개발자 및 AI 에이전트용","다중 작업 흐름 추적 지원"],"es":["Análisis de flujos de trabajo con tecnologías de agente de inteligencia artificial","Depuración de aplicaciones con patrones de ingeniería personalizados","Integración con harness-kit monorepo para una mayor eficiencia","Generación de referencias de depuración compactas para desarrolladores y agentes","Compatibilidad con flujos de trabajo definidos por el usuario"],"fr":["Analyse de flux de travail avec des outils d''agent d''intelligence artificielle","Débogage d''applications avec des modèles d''ingénierie personnalisés","Intégration avec harness-kit monorepo pour une plus grande efficacité","Génération de références de débogage compactes pour les développeurs et les agents","Compatibilité avec des flux de travail définis par l''utilisateur"],"de":["Analyse von Workflows mit KI-Agent-Technologien","Fehlerbehebung von Anwendungen mit benutzerdefinierten Ingenieurmuster","Integration mit harness-kit monorepo für höhere Effizienz","Erzeugung von kompakten Debug-Referenzen für Entwickler und Agenten","Unterstützung von benutzerdefinierten Workflows"],"pt":["Análise de fluxo de trabalho","Referência de depuração compacta","Integração com harness-kit monorepo","Suporte para agentes de Inteligência Artificial","Análise de problemas no código","Suporte para desenvolvedores e agentes"],"ru":["Анализ рабочих процессов","Компактная справка для отладки","Интеграция с harness-kit monorepo","Поддержка ИИ Агентов","Анализ проблем в коде","Поддержка разработчиков и ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["تحليل تدفق العمل","مرجع مدمج للتصحيح","التكامل مع harness-kit monorepo","دعم أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحليل المشكلات في الكود","دعم المطورين وأدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use dk-breadcrumb-creator","dk-breadcrumb-creator setup guide","dk-breadcrumb-creator alternative","dk-breadcrumb-creator vs harness-kit","what is dk-breadcrumb-creator","dk-breadcrumb-creator install"],"zh":["AIエージェント开发工具","工作流程分析","dk-breadcrumb-creator","harness-kit monorepo","AI开发效率","工作流程调试","AIエージェント开发框架"],"ja":["AIエージェント開発ツール","ワークフロー分析","dk-breadcrumb-creator","harness-kit monorepo","AI開発効率","ワークフローデバッグ","AIエージェント開発フレームワーク"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 개발 도구","작업 흐름 분석","dk-breadcrumb-creator","harness-kit monorepo","AI 개발 효율","작업 흐름 디버깅","AI 에이전트 개발 프레임워크"],"es":["dk-breadcrumb-creator","análisis de flujos de trabajo","agentes de inteligencia artificial","depuración de aplicaciones","harness-kit monorepo","patrones de ingeniería","desarrollo de software","inteligencia artificial en el desarrollo de software"],"fr":["dk-breadcrumb-creator","analyse de flux de travail","outils d''agent d''intelligence artificielle","débogage d''applications","harness-kit monorepo","modèles d''ingénierie","développement de logiciels","intelligence artificielle dans le développement de logiciels"],"de":["dk-breadcrumb-creator","Analyse von Workflows","KI-Agent-Technologien","Fehlerbehebung von Anwendungen","harness-kit monorepo","Ingenieurmuster","Software-Entwicklung","Künstliche Intelligenz in der Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["dk-breadcrumb-creator","análise de fluxo de trabalho","Ferramentas de Inteligência Artificial","depuração de código","harness-kit monorepo","desenvolvedores","agentes de Inteligência Artificial","problemas no código"],"ru":["dk-breadcrumb-creator","анализ рабочих процессов","ИИ Агенты","отладка кода","harness-kit monorepo","разработчики","ИИ Агенты","проблемы в коде"],"ar":["dk-breadcrumb-creator","تحليل تدفق العمل","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تصحيح الكود","harness-kit monorepo","المطورون","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","مشكلات في الكود"]}},"owner":"deepklarity","repo":"harness-kit","repoPath":"deepklarity/harness-kit","stars":1,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T21:07:07Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dk-breadcrumb-creator","description":"Traces a workflow end-to-end through the harness-kit monorepo and creates a breadcrumb analysis doc in docs/breadcrumb_analysis/. Use this skill whenever the user wants to document a flow, trace a workflow, understand how a feature works across layers (frontend → backend → worker → CLI), or create debugging guides for a specific flow. Also use when the user mentions breadcrumb, trace this flow, how does X work end to end, document this workflow, or /dk-breadcrumb-creator.","bodyPreview":"# /dk-breadcrumb-creator — Workflow Breadcrumb Analysis\n\nTraces a workflow through the harness-kit monorepo and produces a compact debugging reference. The output is for devs and agents who need to find where things break — not for onboarding docs or architecture overviews.\n\n## Context\n\n<flow_context> $ARGUMENTS </flow_context>\n\nIf the context above is empty, ask: \"Which flow do you want to trace? Describe it in terms of the user action or system event that kicks it off.\"\n\n## Step 0: Check exist","body":"# /dk-breadcrumb-creator — Workflow Breadcrumb Analysis\n\nTraces a workflow through the harness-kit monorepo and produces a compact debugging reference. The output is for devs and agents who need to find where things break — not for onboarding docs or architecture overviews.\n\n## Context\n\n<flow_context> $ARGUMENTS </flow_context>\n\nIf the context above is empty, ask: \"Which flow do you want to trace? Describe it in terms of the user action or system event that kicks it off.\"\n\n## Step 0: Check existing breadcrumbs\n\nBefore scoping anything, read `docs/breadcrumb_analysis/_INDEX.md` to see what already exists. This file lists every breadcrumb folder and what it traces.\n\nCompare the user''s request against the existing entries and make one of three decisions:\n\n1. **Already covered** — The flow is substantially documented in an existing breadcrumb. Tell the user which one covers it and what it contains. Ask if they want to update/extend that existing doc instead of creating a new one.\n\n2. **Partially overlapping** — An existing breadcrumb covers part of the flow (e.g., user asks about \"task execution\" and `spec-task-lifecycle/02-execute-and-dispatch/` covers the dispatch side but not the harness execution internals). Options:\n   - **Extend** the existing breadcrumb (add sections to its FLOW/DETAILS/DEBUG files, or add a new sub-flow folder)\n   - **Create a new breadcrumb** that covers the non-overlapping portion, cross-referencing the existing one\n\n3. **New territory** — Nothing in the index covers this flow. Proceed to Step 1.\n\nWhen extending an existing breadcrumb, read its current FLOW.md first so you don''t duplicate content. Add new information that complements what''s there — don''t rewrite sections that are already accurate.\n\nWhen creating a new breadcrumb that''s adjacent to an existing one, add cross-references in both directions (a \"See also\" line in the new doc pointing to the existing one, and optionally a note in the existing doc pointing to the new one).\n\nPresent your decision to the user before proceeding. Something like:\n\n```\nExisting breadcrumbs I checked:\n- spec-task-lifecycle/02-execute-and-dispatch — covers DAG dispatch, task status transitions\n- harness-isolation-testing — covers harness CLI construction, MCP config, streaming\n\nYour request overlaps with <X> in these areas: <list>.\nI recommend: <extend existing / create new focused on Y / already covered>.\n```\n\n## Step 1: Scope the flow\n\nBefore touching any code, define the boundaries:\n\n```\nFLOW: <name — short, kebab-case, used as folder name>\nTRIGGER: <what kicks it off — button click, API call, CLI command, cron>\nLAYERS: <which layers it touches — fe, api, celery, odin, db>\nEND STATE: <what the user/system sees when it completes>\n```\n\nIf the flow is large (touches 5+ files per layer, or has multiple independent branches), break it into sub-flows. Each sub-flow gets its own folder. Create a parent `_INDEX.md` that links them.\n\nExample of when to split:\n- \"spec execution\" → split into: `spec-planning`, `spec-task-dispatch`, `spec-task-execution`, `spec-assembly`\n- \"task creation\" → probably fine as one flow (FE form → API → DB → response)\n\nAsk the user to confirm the scope before proceeding.\n\n## Step 2: Trace the flow\n\nWork through each layer the flow touches, in execution order. For each hop, record:\n\n1. **Source file and function** — where the action originates\n2. **What it does** — one line, no fluff\n3. **What it passes** — key data (payload shape, IDs, status values)\n4. **Where it goes next** — the next file/function/service in the chain\n\nUse the codebase directly. Read the actual code. Don''t guess from file names.\n\n### Tracing tips\n\n- **Frontend → Backend**: Search for the API URL in the frontend service files (`src/services/`). Match it to the Django URL conf and view.\n- **Backend → Celery**: Search for `.delay(` or `.apply_async(` calls. Check `config/celery.py` and any `tasks.py` files.\n- **Backend → Odin**: Look for `subprocess` calls to `odin` CLI or check `dag_executor.py` for execution strategy routing.\n- **Odin internals**: Follow from `cli.py` → `orchestrator.py` → harness `execute()` methods.\n- **Signal/hook chains**: Check Django signals, DRF `perform_create`/`perform_update` overrides, and model `save()` methods for side effects.\n\n## Step 3: Create the breadcrumb docs\n\nCreate the folder: `docs/breadcrumb_analysis/<flow-name>/`\n\nGenerate three files:\n\n### File 1: `FLOW.md` — High-level flow\n\nThis is the \"where does data go\" overview. Should be readable in 30 seconds.\n\nFormat:\n\n```markdown\n# <Flow Name>\n\nTrigger: <what starts it>\nEnd state: <what the outcome is>\n\n## Flow\n\n<component/file> :: <function>\n  → <what it sends / does>\n<next component/file> :: <function>\n  → <what it sends / does>\n<next component/file> :: <function>\n  → ...\n\n## Sub-flows\n\n(if applicable — link to sub-flow folders)\n```\n\nExample of the flow notation:\n\n```\nBoardView.tsx :: handleCreateTask()\n  → POST /tasks/ {title, board_id, priority, status}\ntasks/views.py :: TaskViewSet.create()\n  → validates, saves to DB, returns TaskReadSerializer response\ntasks/models.py :: Task.save()\n  → triggers TaskHistory creation via signal\n```\n\nKeep it linear. If there''s branching (e.g., different execution strategies), show each branch with a label:\n\n```\ntasks/dag_executor.py :: maybe_execute_task()\n  → checks ODIN_EXECUTION_STRATEGY\n\n  [strategy=local]\n  dag_executor.py :: _execute_local()\n    → subprocess: odin exec <task_id>\n\n  [strategy=celery_dag]\n  execution/celery_dag.py :: poll_and_execute()\n    → picks up task on next poll cycle (every 5s)\n```\n\n### File 2: `DETAILS.md` — Detailed trace\n\nThis is the \"I need to understand what''s actually happening\" doc. File/function level, with the key logic noted.\n\nFormat:\n\n```markdown\n# <Flow Name> — Detailed Trace\n\n## 1. <Layer/Step Name>\n\n**File**: `path/to/file.py`\n**Function**: `function_name()`\n**Called by**: <what triggers this>\n**Calls**: <what this triggers next>\n\nKey logic:\n- <important conditional, validation, transformation>\n- <side effects — signals, logs, cache updates>\n- <error handling — what happens on failure>\n\nData in: <shape of input>\nData out: <shape of output>\n\n---\n\n## 2. <Next Layer/Step>\n...\n```\n\nInclude only details that matter for debugging. Skip boilerplate (imports, standard DRF validation, obvious CRUD). Focus on:\n- Conditionals that change behavior (if/else branches, feature flags, env vars)\n- Data transformations (where shape changes, fields get renamed, data gets enriched)\n- Side effects (signals, async tasks, external calls)\n- Error paths (what exceptions get raised, what gets logged)\n\n### File 3: `DEBUG.md` — Debugging guide\n\nThis is the \"something broke in this flow, where do I look\" doc.\n\nFormat:\n\n```markdown\n# <Flow Name> — Debug Guide\n\n## Log locations\n\n| Layer | Log file | What''s in it |\n|-------|----------|-------------|\n| Django | `taskit/taskit-backend/logs/taskit_detail.log` | Request/response, view errors |\n| DAG exec | `taskit/taskit-backend/logs/dag_exec_<task_id>.log` | Per-task execution log |\n| Odin | `.odin/logs/run_<run_id>.jsonl` | Structured execution events |\n| Celery | terminal output / broker | Task dispatch and results |\n| Frontend | browser console | API call errors, state updates |\n\n(include only rows relevant to this flow)\n\n## What to search for\n\n| Symptom | Where to look | Search term |\n|---------|--------------|-------------|\n| <common failure mode> | <file or log> | <grep pattern> |\n| <another failure mode> | <file or log> | <grep pattern> |\n\n## Quick commands\n\n```bash\n# <description of what this checks>\n<command>\n\n# <description>\n<command>\n```\n\n## Env vars that affect this flow\n\n| Variable | Effect | Default |\n|----------|--------|---------|\n| <VAR_NAME> | <what it changes in this flow> | <default value> |\n\n## Common breakpoints\n\nWhere to put breakpoints or print statements when debugging this flow:\n\n- `path/to/file.py:function_name()` — <why this is a good breakpoint>\n- `path/to/other.py:other_func()` — <why>\n```\n\n### Quick commands section guidance\n\nInclude commands that are actually useful for this specific flow. Examples:\n\n```bash\n# Check if a task exists and its current state\npython taskit/taskit-backend/testing_tools/task_inspect.py <task_id> --brief\n\n# Tail the backend log filtered to a specific task\ngrep \"task_id\" taskit/taskit-backend/logs/taskit_detail.log | tail -20\n\n# Check celery worker status\ncelery -A config inspect active\n\n# Check what odin logged for a spec run\ncat .odin/logs/run_<id>.jsonl | python -m json.tool\n```\n\nDon''t include generic commands. Every command should be specific to debugging THIS flow.\n\n## Step 4: Verify completeness\n\nBefore finishing, check:\n\n- [ ] Every layer the flow touches has at least one entry in FLOW.md\n- [ ] DETAILS.md covers every hop in FLOW.md with file/function specifics\n- [ ] DEBUG.md has log locations for every layer involved\n- [ ] DEBUG.md has at least 3 \"what to search for\" entries based on realistic failure modes\n- [ ] Quick commands actually work (test them if possible)\n- [ ] No fluff — every line earns its place\n- [ ] `docs/breadcrumb_analysis/_INDEX.md` is updated (new folder → add row to the Flows table AND relevant entries to Quick Navigation)\n\n## Step 5: Output summary\n\nAfter creating the docs, tell the user:\n\n```\nCreated breadcrumb analysis for: <flow name>\nLocation: docs/breadcrumb_analysis/<flow-name>/\nFiles:\n  FLOW.md    — high-level flow (<N> steps)\n  DETAILS.md — detailed trace (<N> sections)\n  DEBUG.md   — debug guide (<N> log sources, <N> search patterns, <N> commands)\n\nUpdated: docs/breadcrumb_analysis/_INDEX.md (added to Flows table + Quick Navigation)\n```\n\nIf you extended an existing breadcrumb rather than creating a new folder, adjust the summary accordingly (mention which files were updated and what was added).\n\n## Style rules\n\nThese docs are dev-to-dev notes. They exist so someone (human or agent) can quickly find where to look when something breaks.\n\n- No intro paragraphs. No \"this document describes...\". Jump straight to content.\n- No emoji, no bold-for-emphasis-everywhere, no decorative headers.\n- Use code formatting for file paths, function names, commands, env vars.\n- One line per concept. If a sentence has \"and\" in it, consider splitting.\n- Prefer tables over prose for structured data (log locations, env vars, search patterns).\n- Use `monospace` for anything that appears in code or terminal.\n- If you''re unsure about something, mark it with `[?]` rather than guessing.\n\n## When to split into sub-flows\n\nSplit when:\n- The flow has distinct phases that can fail independently (planning vs execution vs assembly)\n- Different teams/agents own different parts\n- A single FLOW.md would exceed ~50 lines of flow notation\n\nWhen splitting, create:\n```\ndocs/breadcrumb_analysis/<parent-flow>/\n├── _INDEX.md          # Lists sub-flows, brief description of each, execution order\n├── <sub-flow-1>/\n│   ├── FLOW.md\n│   ├── DETAILS.md\n│   └── DEBUG.md\n└── <sub-flow-2>/\n    ├── FLOW.md\n    ├── DETAILS.md\n    └── DEBUG.md\n```\n\nThe `_INDEX.md` format:\n\n```markdown\n# <Parent Flow Name>\n\nSplit into sub-flows because: <one-line reason>\n\n## Sub-flows (execution order)\n\n1. **<sub-flow-1>** — <what this phase does>\n2. **<sub-flow-2>** — <what this phase does>\n\n## Shared context\n\n<any env vars, config, or state that spans all sub-flows>\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-06T07:16:59.050Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for DevOps Agents needing advanced workflow debugging and tracing capabilities through harness-kit monorepo analysis.","zh":"非常适合需要通过harness-kit单体仓库分析进行高级工作流调试和跟踪功能的DevOps代理。","ja":"ハーネスキットモノレポ分析を通じた高度なワークフローのデバッグとトレーシング機能が必要なDevOpsエージェントに最適です。","ko":"하네스 키트 모노레포 분석을 통한 고급 워크플로우 디버깅 및 추적 기능이 필요한 DevOps 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de DevOps que necesitan capacidades de depuración y seguimiento de flujo de trabajo avanzadas a través del análisis de monorepo de harness-kit.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents DevOps ayant besoin de capacités de débogage et de suivi de workflow avancées via l''analyse de monorepo de harness-kit.","de":"Perfekt für DevOps-Agents, die erweiterte Workflow-Debugging- und Nachverfolgungsfunktionen über die Analyse des harness-kit-Monorepos benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes DevOps que precisam de capacidades avançadas de depuração e rastreamento de fluxo de trabalho por meio da análise do monorepo harness-kit.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов DevOps, которым требуются расширенные возможности отладки и отслеживания рабочих процессов посредством анализа монорепозитория harness-kit.","ar":"مثالي لعميلة DevOps الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتصحيح الأخطاء وتحليل سير العمل من خلال تحليل المخزن الواحد harness-kit."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to trace workflows and produce compact debugging references, utilizing context flow analysis and harness-kit integration, enabling efficient identification of workflow breaks through the monorepo.","zh":"赋予代理跟踪工作流和生成紧凑的调试引用、利用上下文流分析和harness-kit集成的能力，从而通过单体仓库实现工作流中断的高效识别。","ja":"エージェントにワークフローをトレースし、コンパクトなデバッグ参照を生成する能力を与え、コンテキストフロー分析とハーネスキットの統合を利用して、モノレポを通じてワークフローのブレークを効率的に特定できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 워크플로우를 추적하고 컴팩트한 디버깅 참조를 생성할 수 있는 기능을 부여하여, 컨텍스트 흐름 분석과 하네스 키트 통합을 利用하여 모노레포를 통해 워크플로우 중단을 효율적으로 식별할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes rastrear flujos de trabajo y producir referencias de depuración compactas, utilizando el análisis de flujo de contexto y la integración de harness-kit, lo que permite la identificación eficiente de interrupciones de flujo de trabajo a través del monorepo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de tracer les flux de travail et de produire des références de débogage compactes, en utilisant l''analyse de flux de contexte et l''intégration de harness-kit, ce qui permet une identification efficace des interruptions de flux de travail via le monorepo.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Workflows nachzuverfolgen und kompakte Debug-Referenzen zu erstellen, indem es Kontextflussanalyse und harness-kit-Integration nutzt, wodurch eine effiziente Identifizierung von Workflow-Unterbrechungen über das Monorepo ermöglicht wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a rastrear fluxos de trabalho e produzir referências de depuração compactas, utilizando análise de fluxo de contexto e integração com harness-kit, permitindo a identificação eficiente de quebras de fluxo de trabalho por meio do monorepo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью отслеживать рабочие процессы и создавать компактные ссылки для отладки, используя анализ контекстного потока и интеграцию с harness-kit, что позволяет эффективно определять разрывы в рабочих процессах посредством монорепозитория.","ar":"يمكن العميل من تتبع سير العمل وتوليد مراجع تصحيح الأخطاء المدمجة، باستخدام تحليل تدفق السياق وتكامل harness-kit، وتمكين تحديد كفء لانقطاع سير العمل من خلال المخزن الواحد."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging workflow breaks in complex monorepo projects","Tracing user action or system event workflows for error identification","Generating compact debugging references for devs and agents"],"zh":["复杂单体仓库项目中的工作流中断调试","用户操作或系统事件工作流以识别错误的跟踪","为开发人员和代理生成紧凑的调试引用"],"ja":["複雑なモノレポプロジェクトでのワークフローブレークのデバッグ","ユーザーアクションまたはシステムイベントのワークフローをエラー識別のためにトレースする","開発者およびエージェントのためのコンパクトなデバッグ参照の生成"],"ko":["복잡한 모노레포 프로젝트의 워크플로우 중단 디버깅","오류 식별을 위한 사용자 동작 또는 시스템 이벤트 워크플로우 추적","개발자 및 에이전트를 위한 컴팩트한 디버깅 참조 생성"],"es":["Depuración de interrupciones de flujo de trabajo en proyectos de monorepo complejos","Rastreo de flujos de trabajo de acciones de usuario o eventos del sistema para la identificación de errores","Generación de referencias de depuración compactas para devs y agents"],"fr":["Débogage des interruptions de flux de travail dans des projets de monorepo complexes","Suivi des flux de travail d''actions utilisateur ou d''événements système pour l''identification d''erreurs","Génération de références de débogage compactes pour les devs et les agents"],"de":["Debugging von Workflow-Unterbrechungen in komplexen Monorepo-Projekten","Nachverfolgung von Benutzeraktionen oder Systemereignis-Workflows zur Fehlernidentifizierung","Erstellung kompakter Debug-Referenzen für Entwickler und Agents"],"pt":["Depuração de quebras de fluxo de trabalho em projetos de monorepo complexos","Rastreamento de fluxos de trabalho de ações de usuário ou eventos do sistema para identificação de erros","Geração de referências de depuração compactas para devs e agentes"],"ru":["Отладка разрывов рабочих процессов в сложных проектах монорепозитория","Отслеживание рабочих процессов пользовательских действий или системных событий для выявления ошибок","Генерация компактных ссылок для отладки для разработчиков и агентов"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء انقطاع سير العمل في مشاريع المخزن الواحد المعقدة","تتبع سير العمل لأحداث المستخدم أو النظام لتحديد الأخطاء","توليد مراجع تصحيح الأخطاء المدمجة للمطورين والعملاء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires harness-kit monorepo integration","Limited to workflow tracing and debugging, not for onboarding or architecture overviews"],"zh":["需要harness-kit单体仓库集成","仅限工作流跟踪和调试，不适用于入门或架构概述"],"ja":["ハーネスキットモノレポ統合が必要","ワークフロートレースとデバッグにのみ限定され、オンボーディングやアーキテクチャの概要には不適"],"ko":["하네스 키트 모노레포 통합이 필요","워크플로우 추적 및 디버깅에만 제한되며, 온보딩 또는 아키텍처 개요에는 적합하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere integración de monorepo de harness-kit","Limitado al seguimiento y depuración de flujos de trabajo, no para la incorporación o la descripción general de la arquitectura"],"fr":["Nécessite l''intégration de monorepo de harness-kit","Limité au suivi et au débogage de flux de travail, et non à l''intégration ou à la description générale de l''architecture"],"de":["Erfordert die Integration des harness-kit-Monorepos","Begrenzt auf Workflow-Nachverfolgung und -Debugging, nicht für Onboarding oder Architekturübersichten"],"pt":["Requer integração do monorepo harness-kit","Limitado ao rastreamento e depuração de fluxo de trabalho, não para integração ou visões gerais da arquitetura"],"ru":["Требует интеграции монорепозитория harness-kit","Ограничен отслеживанием и отладкой рабочих процессов, не подходит для интеграции или обзоров архитектуры"],"ar":["يتطلب تكامل المخزن الواحد harness-kit","محدود برصد وتحليل سير العمل، وليس لمراجعة البنية التحتية أو نظرة عامة على الهندسة المعمارية"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"60c29ae71a590ad296356ccb3344de9d6f373b4608457bfeb59c85eb5136d6ed","qualityScore":45}');
